            <ArticleTitle>Successful treatment of severe arthralgia associated with palmoplantar pustulosis with low-dose oral cyclosporine A.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>512-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two patients with severe arthralgia associated with palmoplantar pustulosis (PPP) were treated with oral cyclosporine A (CsA). Clinical efficacy was assessed on a 0-4 point scale for erythema, desquamation, infiltration, and pustulation, and on a 0-3 point pain scale. Skin lesions and arthralgia improved within twelve weeks with low dose CsA ranging from 2.1 to 2.2 mg/kg/day. High levels of plasma interleukin-6 (IL-6) were reduced to the normal range.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
